          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "правительство (pravítelstvo) — \"the government\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Правительство обещало повысить пенсии. Pravítelstvo obeshchálo povýsit pénsii. The government promised to raise pensions."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Neuter. The cabinet that runs a country; власти is broader."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "правительство (pravítelstvo) is built on правитель \"a ruler\", from править \"to rule, to steer\", from правый \"right\", Proto-Slavic pravŭ \"right, correct\" (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
