          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "власть (vlast) — \"power, authority\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "В этой стране власть часто меняется. V étoy strané vlast chásto menyáyetsya. In this country power often changes hands."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. The plural власти means the authorities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "власть (vlast) \"power, authority\" has the Church Slavonic -ла-: Church Slavonic vlastĭ and native волость both come from Proto-Slavic volstĭ \"rule, power\" (EtymDB). Волость was once a district under someone’s rule."
            }
          ]
        },
